                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                        "entry_id": "08536eea-4c1e-37ed-877f-8516c8384348",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A widespread chain of coffee shops."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "36458511-bcdc-4fd9-b70e-a9a2b35ace7c",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Each week, more than 33 million folks worldwide pass through a Starbucks. Plus, up to three Starbucks open every day somewhere on the globe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0fd6eae-b89b-492f-9b75-e799e726d7eb",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Consider the Starbucks effect in the slogans written up recently in Fast Company magazine, where companies from various sectors now aspire to be the 'Starbucks of their respective industry': ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44936c73-7321-4be4-8633-c0ffa918f1f4",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "On my three-block walk to the subway I noticed not one, not two, but four Starbucks, which was quite a high concentration of retail outlets even for the Queen of Caffeine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e276404a-e48e-4435-8eb3-438cb034f574",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Companies now want to turn themselves into “the Starbucks of the ham business” or “the Starbucks of fuel-injector makers.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14222352-09ef-46ca-98be-620c7f08985f",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Many people began to wonder whether we really needed two Starbucks directly across the street from each other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1782e56-b687-43b6-924d-9708612a15d4",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Said the CEO of the nearly 500-plus store Caribou Coffee chain, “I got into the business because of what they [Starbucks] created.” In China, a small chain, Real Brewed Tea, aims to be “the Starbucks of tea.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8b95ac0-12d5-49fe-b152-76cf1aa62de2",
                                "sense_id": "8e9c56a5-6584-354d-b2b0-30f219f07e24",
                                "text": "Also returning is Pumpkin Cream Cold Brew, an iced-drink topped with pumpkin cream cold foam and a dusting of pumpkin spice that Starbucks launched in 2019."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
